  [FAIL] C12 [VERDICT] L10's exclusion of c_s^2 = 1/3 by gravitational Cherenkov is correct AS STATED (bound 2e-15, exclusion 2.1e14x, exp wall cannot rescue)   (it is not.  The bound is 7e+05x weaker than stated, and the exp wall DOES rescue the gate once it is evaluated where the radiation is generated rather than along the ambient path.  Handoff A5 must be rewritten as a conditional.  The lead's construction is ALIVE with a subluminal clock IF its clock-matter coupling screens at high acceleration -- which its own static branch says it does -- and only then; sigma = 1 is NOT forced by Cherenkov as things stand)

